You are analyzing an Upwork job post to extract structured requirements.
Your analysis will be used by other specialists to evaluate fit and write a proposal.

## Job Post to Analyze

{{ job_post_text }}

## Your Task

Extract the following information from the job post above. Be precise and thorough.
If a piece of information is not explicitly stated, make a reasonable inference and
mark it as "[inferred]".

Respond in EXACTLY this format:

### Skills Required
- List each technical skill, framework, language, or tool mentioned or implied
- Include both hard requirements and "nice to have" skills

### Project Type
- Categorize: Web App / Mobile App / Desktop App / API/Backend / Data/AI/ML / 
  Design / Other
- Brief description of what they're building

### Estimated Budget
- State the budget if mentioned (fixed price or hourly rate + estimated hours)
- If not mentioned, infer from project complexity: Low ($100-500) / Medium ($500-2000) / High ($2000+)

### Client Tone
- Categorize: Professional / Casual / Urgent / Detail-oriented / Vague
- Note any personality cues (e.g., "we're a startup", "enterprise client", "need it ASAP")

### Key Requirements
- List the 3-5 most critical requirements that a proposal MUST address
- These are the deal-breakers — what the client cares about most

### Red Flags (if any)
- Unrealistic expectations, scope creep risks, or concerning patterns
